    ("What is the classic '100 prisoners and light bulb' / 'Blue-eyed islanders': On an island with N blue-eyed people who never discuss eye color, if a visitor says 'At least one of you has blue eyes', on which night do all N blue-eyed islanders deduce it and leave?", "Night N", ["Night 1", "Night N-1", "Never"], "By mathematical induction: N=1 leaves Night 1; N=2 leaves Night 2; N blue-eyed islanders leave on Night N."),
    ("In the '100 prisoners & 100 boxes' loop strategy, each prisoner may open 50 boxes following the cycle of numbers inside. Roughly what probability do all 100 succeed together?", "Over 31% (1 - ln 2)", ["(1/2)^100", "50%", "1%"], "They succeed iff the random permutation has no cycle longer than 50, which happens with probability 1 - (1/51 + ... + 1/100) ≈ 31.18%."),
