    ("Which famous 1736 graph-theory problem by Leonhard Euler proved why you cannot cross all 7 bridges of Königsberg exactly once?", "Eulerian path condition (at most 2 odd-degree vertices)", ["Hamiltonian cycle NP-completeness", "Four Color Theorem", "Planar Kuratowski test"], "All four landmasses had odd bridge counts (3, 3, 3, 5), making a single crossing impossible."),
